# ADR 0001 — Session revocation

- **Status:** Proposed
- **Date:** 2026-09-27
- **Decider:** lpheng104 (repository owner Git identity; preferred name pending)
- **Requirements affected:** FR-AUTH-02, FR-ACCESS-01, NFR-SEC-01
- **Related ADRs:** 0002, 0003

## Context

FR-AUTH-02 requires logout to revoke the server-side session. The existing app stores a random token in its signed cookie and resolves it through the session collection. A stolen pre-logout cookie must not restore access.

The student has used Flask and MongoDB. This review retains those tools under CON-05 and compares two session designs. SP-01 is a bounded local experiment; its mock database cannot establish hosted consistency. Reserve 1 hour for security review and share the 2-hour hosted spike with the deployment decision.

## Options considered

| Option | Weighted score | The detail that decided it |
|---|---:|---|
| database-token | 4.55 | SP-01 rejects replay in 10/10 trials. |
| signed-cookie-only | 2.25 | SP-01 control accepts replay in 10/10 trials; fails the revocation gate. |

Scores and method: [technology evaluation](../tech-evaluation.md).

## Decision

I will retain database-backed token revocation and current per-request membership checks, subject to student acceptance of this proposed record. Use the existing pinned Flask/PyMongo implementation; exact hosted runtime compatibility remains a deployment check. Cookie-only authentication without revocation state is not acceptable for FR-AUTH-02.

## Consequences

**Positive**

- Logout invalidates the server token, supporting FR-AUTH-02.
- Current membership remains the authority for FR-ACCESS-01.

**Negative**

- Database unavailability blocks authenticated requests; budget 1 hour to review error paths and expiry behavior.
- Session records need lifecycle cleanup. The current source checks expiration on reads but does not create a sessions TTL index; do not claim automatic physical deletion is verified.
- Local mock success does not establish hosted security; spend the shared 2-hour SP-02 budget verifying that seam.

## Revisit trigger

Write a superseding ADR if any 1 replay accesses protected content after logout, or session lookup adds more than 150 ms to warm p95 in the NFR-PERF-01 dataset.

